Task: Your task is to implement a base `Spell` class and two specialized spell classes: `Fireball` and `IceShard`. Each spell type should have a unique casting behavior by overriding the `cast()` method from the base class. Focus on clearly defining constructors and ensuring the `cast()` method returns descriptive strings for easy testing.

Submitted code:
```
class Spell {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  cast() {
    // Provides a fallback message if a subclass doesn't override it
    return `Casting ${this.name}...`;
  }
}

class Fireball extends Spell {
  constructor(name, damage) {
    // Calls the parent constructor to set this.name
    super(name);
    this.damage = damage;
  }

  cast() {
    // Overrides generic message with specific Fireball logic
    return `${this.name} erupts, dealing ${this.damage} fire damage!`;
  }
}

class IceShard extends Spell {
  constructor(name, frostEffect) {
    // Calls the parent constructor to set this.name
    super(name);
    this.frostEffect = frostEffect;
  }

  cast() {
    // Overrides generic message with specific IceShard logic
    return `${this.name} strikes with a ${this.frostEffect} touch, freezing the target.`;
  }
}

// --- Example Usage ---
const genericSpell = new Spell("Mystic Bolt");
const fireball = new Fireball("Inferno Blast", 50);
const iceShard = new IceShard("Frost Nova", "chilling");

console.log(genericSpell.cast()); // Casting Mystic Bolt...
console.log(fireball.cast());     // Inferno Blast erupts, dealing 50 fire damage!
console.log(iceShard.cast());     // Frost Nova strikes with a chilling touch, freezing the target.

```

